<title>JAPAN: Japan June soybean crushing up 11.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan June soybean crushing up 11.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's soybean crushing in June reached 322,085 tonnes, up 11.9 percent from a year earlier, and rapeseed crushing totalled 182,051 tonnes, up 12.0 percent from June 1996, Agriculture Ministry data showed.</p>
<p>The country's output of soy oil during June was 58,410 tonnes and that of soymeal 246,273 tonnes, it showed.</p>
<p>The following are details of the ministry's imported oilseeds crushing and stock data (in tonnes):</p>
<p> - Soybeans -  June 97	June 96    Jan-June 97  Jan-June 96</p>
<p> Crushing	322,085	287,691     1,860,769    1,800,396</p>
<p> Oil output     58,410	 52,882	 334,158	325,329</p>
<p> Meal output   246,273	221,247     1,420,740    1,389,889</p>
<p>- Rapeseed -</p>
<p> Crushing	182,051	162,600     1,001,046	962,583</p>
<p> Oil output     76,652	 69,263	 420,846	409,969</p>
<p> Meal output   103,301	 91,991	 562,756	543,586</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
